1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:04,600
So, we know the Labour Law sets the rules,

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:07,500
but who makes sure companies
actually follow them?

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:09,950
That's where MOHRE comes in.

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:14,250
MOHRE stands for the Ministry of
Human Resources and Emiratisation.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:19,080
It's the main government authority overseeing
private-sector employment under UAE

6
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,770
federal labour legislation.

7
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:25,970
It manages employment services, issues
work permits, oversees compliance,

8
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:29,470
and can take action when employers
fail to meet their obligations.

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,990
But MOHRE doesn't work alone.

10
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,370
Several government systems
support the employment framework.

11
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:39,490
First, the Wage Protection System, or WPS.

12
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:44,410
The electronic system used to process
and monitor employee wage payments,

13
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:48,370
helping ensure employees are paid
the correct amount and on time.

14
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:53,450
Employers who fail to meet their obligations
may face penalties or restrictions.

15
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:58,700
Nafis is a government initiative that supports
the employment and professional development

16
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,670
of Emirati nationals in the private sector.

17
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:06,690
ILOE, the Involuntary
Loss of Employment scheme.

18
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:11,420
This is an unemployment insurance scheme
that provides temporary financial support

19
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:14,870
to eligible employees who
lose their jobs involuntarily.

20
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:20,870
It is mandatory for employees covered by the
scheme, although eligibility and exclusions apply.

21
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:27,490
Each plays a different role, but together they
help support and regulate employment in the UAE.

22
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:32,410
And for HR, compliance means more than
simply knowing these systems exist.

23
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,070
You need to make sure your
company's processes are working.
